WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:05.138
- Hello. I'm Gav.
- I'm chilly.

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:07.240
You look chilly.
Welcome to "Planet Slo Mo."

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.642
Today we're in a very chilly
Seoul, South Korea.

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:12.779
I feel like in the past,
Dan, we've filmed a lot
of very impressive animals

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.781
doing very impressive things
in slo-mo.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.115
You know what else
is impressive, though?

00:00:16.148 --> 00:00:18.317
- Go on.
- Humans.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.320
- I mean, not us, though.
  Specifically not us.
- Humans that aren't us.

00:00:21.353 --> 00:00:23.322
- Yeah.
- That's correct.

00:00:23.355 --> 00:00:25.658
We're here to film
the Kukkiwon Taekwondo
Demonstration Team.

00:00:25.691 --> 00:00:27.126
Taekwondo--
invented in Korea,

00:00:27.159 --> 00:00:29.262
so by now they're
pretty good at it.

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:31.297
- They've had enough time
  to get expert on it.
- Yeah, I think so.

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:35.668
I've seen the clips
of this demonstration team
on YouTube, and it is nuts.

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:38.171
The amount of height
they can get--
I can't wait to see it.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.173
I think we should go
and get into the arena,

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.542
set up the Phantom,
film some crazy stuff.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.044
- I'm up for it.
- All right. Let's go.

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:05.531
( shouting )

00:01:05.564 --> 00:01:08.134
So here we are
in the taekwondo arena.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.837
There's some
audience seating and stuff.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:15.374
However, this light
is completely unsuitable
for shooting high-speed.

00:01:15.407 --> 00:01:17.477
It's actually very dim
on the Phantom camera,

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.378
and it flickers like crazy.

00:01:19.411 --> 00:01:21.714
So we went a little bit
mental with the lights,

00:01:21.747 --> 00:01:23.783
and we've got a bunch of 18Ks.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:25.718
We've got all these
Dinos at the back

00:01:25.751 --> 00:01:27.220
that should look really cool.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.722
So why don't
we bring up the lights?

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:32.658
This is a grand total--
it's going to be a grand total

00:01:32.691 --> 00:01:37.163
of over 145,000 watts
of light.

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:39.866
Like, back in the day,
when you used to have
the incandescent bulbs,

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.868
you'd be like,
"Oof. Got a 40-watter there."

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:45.138
- Ooh, yeah.
- "Ooh, a 100-watt bulb?
  Are you kidding?"

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.874
- One of these is 18,000 watts.
- I can already feel the heat.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:50.409
It takes awhile
to get up to strength.

00:01:50.442 --> 00:01:52.411
I think we're on--
well on the way.

00:01:52.444 --> 00:01:55.748
Probably get maybe a 2-8,
1,000 frames a second?

00:01:55.781 --> 00:01:58.251
- Yeah.
- It should be lovely.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.253
Gav: Okay, I think we're ready
to bring out the team,

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.255
film some kicking
and flying through
the air and that.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:03.723
- Can't wait.
- All right. Let's do it.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:06.225
Okay, so we're at
1,000 frames a second.

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:08.427
We can only record
for five seconds,

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:09.896
so I think we'll get
the tail end of it,

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:12.431
and this move is going to be
just a bunch of roundhouses.

00:02:12.464 --> 00:02:13.766
- Okay.
- It should be good.

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:15.168
- Sounds good.
- All right, let's do it.

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:16.636
( shouting )

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:26.279
- Whoa.
- ( shouting )

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.780
( gasps )

00:02:27.813 --> 00:02:29.682
I mean, they just
destroyed the equivalent

00:02:29.715 --> 00:02:32.218
of what's probably
a kitchen table
with their feet

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:34.287
in about five seconds there.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.955
- That was kind of scary.
- Look at this.

00:02:35.988 --> 00:02:39.292
Dan: Flip.

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.627
Gav: It's, like, heel--
 like, ball.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:44.297
Dan: You see the powder from
 the wood just get smashed?

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.832
Gav: Just sailing off
 into the distance.

00:02:49.568 --> 00:02:51.470
Dan: Absolutely annihilated
 that piece of wood
 with his heel.

00:02:51.503 --> 00:02:53.373
Gav: There's just
 splinters everywhere.

00:02:56.508 --> 00:02:58.511
Dan:
 That would really hurt.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:02:59.579
Gav: I feel like that
 would bloody hurt.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.314
Dan:
 Just smashing...

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:02.682
Gav:
 Then it hits his hand.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.653
He actually kicked
 the one from before.

00:03:07.686 --> 00:03:09.255
Dan: It was still the air
 from the previous kick.

00:03:09.288 --> 00:03:10.690
That's how quick it is.

00:03:12.691 --> 00:03:14.660
Yeah, that looks nice
 when the wood bursts

00:03:14.693 --> 00:03:16.963
with the backlight,
 that sawdust.

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.698
I wonder how many trees
 they've gone through?

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:21.734
Gav: And then
 big old final kick.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:22.969
Dan: You got to remember,
 they've just kicked,

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.837
like, six pieces of wood,

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:26.873
and then that one's higher
 than the other guy's head.

00:03:31.543 --> 00:03:33.846
A double spin.

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:36.883
Gav: Look at the levels
 of adjustment there.

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.353
Bloody epic.

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:41.387
Dan:
 That is impressive.

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:47.526
Have you ever jumped
and kicked three things
before landing?

00:03:47.559 --> 00:03:48.794
Uh, no,
I've mostly kicked

00:03:48.827 --> 00:03:51.697
one thing, I think,
but never three.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.699
- We're about to learn
  how it's done.
- All right.

00:03:53.732 --> 00:03:55.235
( shouting )

00:03:57.569 --> 00:03:58.671
( shouts )

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:01.874
I love the look
to camera there,
as well, afterwards.

00:04:01.907 --> 00:04:02.909
That was great.

00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:09.015
Gav: I feel like
 you would do that,

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:11.017
and you'd hurt the foot.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:14.887
Dan:
 Man, that's so close
 to his face.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:17.923
Look at curled
 and straight her feet are
 as she's in the air here.

00:04:17.956 --> 00:04:19.792
Gav: It looks like,
 you know when you see in films

00:04:19.825 --> 00:04:21.427
that people are on wires
 just sailing through the air

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:23.429
kicking through--
 it looks like that.

00:04:23.462 --> 00:04:25.398
Just walking through the air.
 It's like someone's swimming.

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:27.566
Dan: It is.
 It's like there's a set
 of stairs there.

00:04:27.599 --> 00:04:29.402
Gav:
 Making use of each foot.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.970
"I kicked with that leg.
 I'll kick with this now."

00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:32.571
Dan:
 Oh, one after the other.

00:04:32.604 --> 00:04:33.806
And the last one,
 she's on her way down.

00:04:33.839 --> 00:04:35.574
- Gav: Oh! 
- Dan: Bang.

00:04:35.607 --> 00:04:39.912
Gav: Look at that.
 Right in front of his face.

00:04:39.945 --> 00:04:41.380
Dan:
 I wonder how many times
 they've been hit

00:04:41.413 --> 00:04:42.615
in the face
 with that thing.

00:04:44.983 --> 00:04:47.987
I think it's time we move on
to some aerial stuff.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.056
Wasn't that aerial?
She was in the air,
kicked three boards.

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:52.692
She was in the air,
but she wasn't in the air.

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:55.428
Yeah? All right. Okay.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:56.595
I'm talking humans
taking flight.

00:04:56.628 --> 00:04:57.930
I'm intrigued.
I'm intrigued.

00:04:57.963 --> 00:05:00.433
- Yeah. All right.
- ( shouting )

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:01.901
Look at the braced positions.

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:07.006
Whoa!

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:09.075
Got some air.

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:11.043
Wood went, like,
40 feet in the air there.

00:05:11.076 --> 00:05:12.745
It's an absolute hazard.

00:05:12.778 --> 00:05:15.448
They got showered in wood.

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:21.787
Yeah, look. You see the
 spring-loaded procedure here.

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:24.457
Gav: There's two people
 being springboards.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.625
He's being supported
 by the guy behind.

00:05:26.658 --> 00:05:29.095
Dan: I think the second guy
 is just to support the bar.

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:31.630
Whereas the front person
 is doing a power squat

00:05:31.663 --> 00:05:33.666
- to shove them into the air. 
- Gav: Yeah.

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:36.936
What an amazing sight.

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:38.804
Dan: Got some
 serious air there.

00:05:38.837 --> 00:05:39.872
Gav: Oh!

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:43.976
- Dan: That is madness. 
- What?

00:05:44.009 --> 00:05:45.711
Dan: It looks like
 they're in zero G right now.

00:05:45.744 --> 00:05:47.079
They could be in space.

00:05:47.112 --> 00:05:48.948
This guy here
 looks like an astronaut

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:51.017
just in the space station,
 just chilling out.

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:53.986
Gav:
 Look at that.

00:05:54.019 --> 00:05:55.488
Dan:
 Look at all the powder
 and the sawdust

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:57.656
coming out
 from the wood there.

00:05:57.689 --> 00:05:59.992
Gav:
 That is so impressive.

00:06:00.025 --> 00:06:02.995
That's like someone's house
exploded and the roof blew off.

00:06:03.028 --> 00:06:06.999
Just raining pieces
 and people and wood.

00:06:07.032 --> 00:06:09.668
- Dan: That's wicked. 
- Okay, so this one,

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:11.437
- four paddles.
- Yeah?

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:13.506
Three on the way up,
and for good measure,

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:16.008
- one on the way down.
- Well, that's just greedy,
  for a start.

00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:19.011
He's going to get
three in mid-air, and then
get one on the way down?

00:06:19.044 --> 00:06:22.081
Three up, and then
at the apex, he's like,
"I need one more."

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:26.018
Just one day he was like,
"I can get four here.
I can do that."

00:06:26.051 --> 00:06:28.988
All right.
Looks like they're ready.

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:30.890
( shouting )

00:06:37.729 --> 00:06:39.799
- Dan: Whoa!
- ( shouts )

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:42.535
Flippin-A'.

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:44.703
- God.
- GoPro's still
  in one piece.

00:06:44.736 --> 00:06:49.175
Four pieces of wood
separated by about 12 feet,

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:51.544
just smashed in about
less than a second.

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:56.882
Gav: So he bashes it
 with his hand.

00:06:56.915 --> 00:06:58.150
Dan: Bang.

00:06:58.183 --> 00:06:59.819
Gav: That one gets
 the left foot.

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:01.086
- Dan: Two. 
- That one gets the right.

00:07:01.119 --> 00:07:03.189
Dan: Oh!
 That one's annihilated.

00:07:03.222 --> 00:07:06.892
He's in mid-air doing
 a weird half-flip twist.

00:07:06.925 --> 00:07:08.594
And then he's like, "All right,
 I got to hit this now."

00:07:09.928 --> 00:07:12.731
Oh, he's hit the metal
 there as well.

00:07:12.764 --> 00:07:15.901
Gav: That's got to have
 been slightly painful.

00:07:15.934 --> 00:07:17.736
Dan:
 That is savage.

00:07:17.769 --> 00:07:20.206
I like how he absolutely
 started out like,

00:07:20.239 --> 00:07:23.008
"Ow. But I'm not going to
 show any pain here."

00:07:23.041 --> 00:07:26.712
All right, this one, Dan,
it's a backflip with all
the kicks in the world.

00:07:26.745 --> 00:07:28.914
He's going to kick
all the way around.

00:07:28.947 --> 00:07:31.517
That's 1, 2, 3,
4, 5, 6, 7, 8.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:33.586
Last time it was four,
and I thought that was greedy.

00:07:33.619 --> 00:07:35.955
- Now this is eight.
- ( shouting )

00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:37.756
Yeah, he's got this.

00:07:37.789 --> 00:07:40.025
He'll run up.

00:07:40.058 --> 00:07:41.627
- Oh, yes!
- ( shouting )

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:42.761
- That was awesome.
- Did you hear it?

00:07:42.794 --> 00:07:44.930
He nailed it.
It was so satisfying.

00:07:44.963 --> 00:07:46.765
- It was over in a second.
- Done.

00:07:46.798 --> 00:07:49.001
- Sounded like a machine gun.
- That was awesome.

00:07:52.804 --> 00:07:54.940
Gav:
 Look at this. One.

00:07:54.973 --> 00:07:56.609
Dan: He's putting power
 into these kicks as well.

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:58.611
Gav: Two.
 And the thing is,

00:07:58.644 --> 00:07:59.945
I can imagine
 that would be hard

00:07:59.978 --> 00:08:02.114
if you actually
 had a solid surface.

00:08:02.147 --> 00:08:04.783
But these are
 giving him nothing.
 He's just kicking them.

00:08:04.816 --> 00:08:07.119
Dan:
 You see how his foot stops
 just before that board

00:08:07.152 --> 00:08:09.121
in order to get
 the maximum amount

00:08:09.154 --> 00:08:11.724
of power and rotation
 into the kick?

00:08:11.757 --> 00:08:13.792
Gav:
 Kicked the last one.

00:08:13.825 --> 00:08:15.261
Dan: And he's got
 one more to get.

00:08:15.294 --> 00:08:16.795
Gav: And he bloody
 got it as well.

00:08:16.828 --> 00:08:17.830
Dan:
 Got it as well.

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:24.637
Going to try
a very close, very wide,

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:27.640
- and very handheld shot.
- Very scary shot.

00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:28.974
I'm going to jam in here

00:08:29.007 --> 00:08:30.976
and I'm going to go
track it all the way around

00:08:31.009 --> 00:08:33.646
and see if I can get it.
It's ambitious.

00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:35.281
It's ambitious.
I feel kind of intimidated

00:08:35.314 --> 00:08:36.916
being this close to it,
as well.

00:08:36.949 --> 00:08:37.983
Yeah, might get hit
in the head with a board.

00:08:38.016 --> 00:08:39.051
- Dan: Yeah.
- We'll see.

00:08:39.084 --> 00:08:40.953
All right,
I think we're good.

00:08:40.986 --> 00:08:42.821
( shouting )

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:48.794
( shouting )

00:08:48.827 --> 00:08:50.996
I nearly took one
to the face there.

00:08:51.029 --> 00:08:52.932
God.

00:08:52.965 --> 00:08:56.202
- Looks promising.
- Promising, indeed.

00:09:00.706 --> 00:09:03.008
- Dan: Goodness me. 
- That is a mad shot.

00:09:03.041 --> 00:09:05.177
Dan: You got the flags
 in the background.

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:06.645
It's clearly
 someone upside-down

00:09:06.678 --> 00:09:08.180
at least ten feet in the air

00:09:08.213 --> 00:09:11.717
kicking things eight times
 in less than a second.

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:16.689
Gav: Look at that
 flair at the end.

00:09:16.722 --> 00:09:18.857
Dan:
 Just for extra good measure.

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:21.026
That's what you call
 an action shot.

00:09:21.059 --> 00:09:23.362
- Gav: That was cool. 
- It's awesome.

00:09:23.395 --> 00:09:26.999
For a finale, we asked them,

00:09:27.032 --> 00:09:29.068
"How high can you
send someone?"

00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:33.339
And they've come up
with this sort of
multi-stage launch system.

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:35.007
This should be
bloody impressive.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:37.076
- ( shouting )
- Multi-stage launch.

00:09:37.109 --> 00:09:38.678
Ready.

00:09:41.747 --> 00:09:45.217
- Whoa!
- Aw, flip! And the landing
  he nailed, as well.

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:47.720
That was insane.
That was so good.

00:09:47.753 --> 00:09:51.724
That was--
that was so ridiculous.

00:09:51.757 --> 00:09:54.660
When you think about--
that's just launched

00:09:54.693 --> 00:09:56.729
from his legs
off various items there.

00:09:56.762 --> 00:10:00.065
I wonder what he squats,
because that is some serious
power in his legs there.

00:10:00.098 --> 00:10:01.267
"Uh, mate,
what are you squatting?"

00:10:10.275 --> 00:10:13.379
I think he got more
 of a powerful kick there
 than I've seen today.

00:10:13.412 --> 00:10:16.415
And the piece of wood
 almost hit the flags
 on the roof.

00:10:16.448 --> 00:10:18.083
Dan:
 Look how far he's falling.

00:10:18.116 --> 00:10:19.285
Gav: Look at how far
 he's going there.

00:10:22.287 --> 00:10:25.758
It seems to be on the chest,
 onto the arms.

00:10:25.791 --> 00:10:27.926
- Dan:
  This is the main launch. 
- Double push.

00:10:27.959 --> 00:10:31.096
And then he seems to use
 both feet on the next--

00:10:31.129 --> 00:10:35.401
No, it's just one foot.
 It's just one foot on each.

00:10:35.434 --> 00:10:37.770
It's like he's going up
 what looks to be

00:10:37.803 --> 00:10:39.972
two flights of stairs
 in two steps.

00:10:45.143 --> 00:10:47.413
Dan:
 He gets some serious power
 into this kick as well.

00:10:47.446 --> 00:10:50.115
- Gav: He kicked
  that to the moon. 
- Shatters it.

00:10:50.148 --> 00:10:56.121
Gav:
 He is at probably roof height
 on an English house.

00:10:56.154 --> 00:10:58.123
Dan: He'd be knocking
 out the satellite dish
 at this point.

00:10:58.156 --> 00:10:59.325
Gav: Yeah.

00:11:01.159 --> 00:11:03.829
Okay, look how far
 he's falling here.

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:08.300
That is absolutely insane.

00:11:08.333 --> 00:11:09.835
Lovely stuff.

00:11:11.336 --> 00:11:13.305
Well, that's it.
I feel like we've got

00:11:13.338 --> 00:11:14.973
some really good
footage there,

00:11:15.006 --> 00:11:16.408
but I've never felt
so worthless

00:11:16.441 --> 00:11:17.976
- in all my life.
- So inadequate.

00:11:18.009 --> 00:11:21.146
Yeah, just incapable
of what humans can do.

00:11:21.179 --> 00:11:23.816
How long do you think
it would take you
to get to this point?

00:11:23.849 --> 00:11:27.986
Do you think if
you trained for 10,000 hours,
you could do that?

00:11:28.019 --> 00:11:30.823
No, 10,000 hours wouldn't
get me close to this.

00:11:30.856 --> 00:11:33.425
Oh. I can do it.

00:11:33.458 --> 00:11:36.995
To think that earlier
there was a bloke

00:11:37.028 --> 00:11:39.832
just way up above
where we stood now.

00:11:39.865 --> 00:11:43.268
They were moving so fast
and covering so much
distance through the air

00:11:43.301 --> 00:11:45.838
that I was actually
struggling with the refresh
rate on the monitor.

